This product includes data derived from third-party software:

models/bragg_generic.npz
    Depth-dose curves, lateral kernels and spot widths exported from the
    "Generic" proton machine (protons_Generic.mat) as distributed with pyRadPlan
    (https://github.com/e0404/pyRadPlan) under the BSD 3-Clause License
    reproduced below. The machine data originates from matRad
    (https://github.com/e0404/matRad).

    Its "hlut" array is the HU-to-density table ("hu_to_density") published
    in beam_parameters.json of the DoseRAD2026 dataset
    (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19347848), licensed CC BY-NC 4.0.

submission/app.py
    Follows the DoseRAD2026 example algorithm published by the challenge
    (https://github.com/chrisvanrun/DoseRAD2026-example-algorithm-invoke-API).
    The file implements the interface the platform requires -- a FastAPI app
    with /health and /invoke -- and is kept close to that example so the
    contract is recognisable.

evaluation/metrics.py
    Ports the beam MAE and IDD-distance arithmetic of the challenge's
    evaluation code (https://github.com/DoseRAD2026/evaluation-setup), so that
    local scores equal the platform's exactly.

    Neither upstream repository carries a licence. To the extent these two files
    reproduce the organisers' code, they are not covered by this repository's
    Apache-2.0 licence.

